</section>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } .hero-img { max-height: 320px; } }
</style>
<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Garage building in Airdrie usually starts the same way: a 1990s to 2020s house with a front attached garage, a rear lane, and a backyard that could hold a second building. Some owners want a workshop or space for a truck, some want the cars off the street before winter, and some just want a place for the bikes and the snow tires.</p><p>Back Lane Garage Co is an advertising site. It puts Airdrie homeowners in touch with independent garage builders, who quote and contract directly with you. We do not build, pull permits or hold a licence ourselves. Call (403) 555-0162 now and ask to be matched with builders who quote in Airdrie.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Airdrie</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Airdrie Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Detached garages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A single, double or triple garage on the lane side of an Airdrie lot, priced by an independent builder from your real property report. Start with the <a href="/detached-garages/">detached garage page</a> for what a quote should list.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Garage packages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A fixed-scope package can make quotes easier to compare, as long as you ask exactly what it includes. Read <a href="/garage-packages/">garage packages</a> before you set one beside a line-by-line quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Custom and oversized garages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Extra height, extra depth or a workshop bay for a truck or hobby project changes the design, and the City will want to see it on the plans. Builders quote these one at a time; see <a href="/custom-garages/">custom garages</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Garage replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If an older detached garage on an Airdrie lot has worn out, removal and rebuild can be quoted together or separately. Ask each builder to state which one they are pricing; see <a href="/garage-replacement/">garage replacement</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .feat-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } }
</style>
  </div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">What the City of Airdrie asks for</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The City of Airdrie's garage page says permits are required for all new garages and sheds over 10 square metres (107 square feet). An application needs a Real Property Report showing the proposed garage and its setbacks, plus a building plan. The City also says that starting work before the permit is issued may result in permit fees being doubled.</p><p>Height is capped at 5 metres (16 feet 5 inches) from ground to peak, or the height of the house, whichever is smaller. The page also says walls closer than 1.2 metres (4 feet) to the property line are not permitted to have windows, doors or vent openings. Walls closer than 600 millimetres (2 feet) must have a minimum 45 minute fire resistance rating on the inside face, and soffits may not project closer than 450 millimetres (18 inches) to the line.</p><p>As of 1 March 2026, the City says all truss specifications must carry the seal and signature of an Alberta Registered Engineer. Contractors must hold valid trade qualification certificates and an Airdrie business licence. Ask the City whether your plan also needs a development permit and what the fees are, and confirm with the City of Airdrie before you sign anything.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">What builders advertise for an Airdrie garage</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The only Airdrie-specific prices we have are advertised by BVM Builders on its Airdrie page, read on 29 September 2026. The page does not say whether GST is included. It lists:</p><ul><li>Single garage, 16 by 20: $55,000 to $85,000</li><li>Double garage, 22 by 22: $82,000 to $125,000</li><li>Double garage, 22 by 24: $88,000 to $135,000</li><li>Triple garage, 32 by 26: $135,000 to $200,000</li></ul><p>These are one builder's advertised ranges, not a market average and not a quote from this site. The spread inside a single row shows how much depends on the finish, the foundation and what is included, so ask every builder to put the same items in writing. Our <a href="/garage-building-cost-calgary/">garage cost page</a> shows what other Calgary-area builders advertise, for comparison.</p><p>Three written quotes that list the same scope let you compare builders on the work, not on the headline number. Check that each quote says who applies for the permits, who supplies the Real Property Report, and what happens to the price if the City asks for changes.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Timing, hail and getting quotes before spring</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Falcon Contracting, a Calgary builder, says a standard garage build takes 4 to 8 weeks from excavation to inspection, though permits and weather can affect that. Hammerhead Construction, another Calgary builder, says more projects are completed in the summer months, so demand for product and labour can be higher in busy periods. Those are builders' statements, not a promise for any Airdrie job. If you want a garage ready for summer, gathering quotes over winter is the easy way to do it.</p><p>Winter building is possible too, but both builders say cold-weather concrete work can add heating costs. Ask each builder how they would handle a spring start and what the quote assumes.</p><p>Hail is common here. The Insurance Bureau of Canada reported that the 13 June 2020 storm that hit Calgary, Airdrie, Rocky View County and the surrounding area caused almost $1.2 billion in insured damage. It is reasonable to ask every builder what roofing and siding their quote includes. For nearby towns, see <a href="/garage-builders-cochrane/">Cochrane</a> and <a href="/garage-builders-rocky-view-county/">Rocky View County</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F3F2EE;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do I need a permit for a detached garage in Airdrie?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">The City of Airdrie says permits are required for all new garages and sheds over 10 square metres (107 square feet). You will need a Real Property Report showing the proposed garage and setbacks, plus a building plan. Confirm the details, including whether a development permit applies to your lot, with the City before building.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">How close to my property line can a garage have windows or doors in Airdrie?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">The City of Airdrie says walls closer than 1.2 metres (4 feet) to the property line cannot have windows, doors or vent openings. Walls closer than 600 millimetres (2 feet) need a minimum 45 minute fire resistance rating on the inside face. Check your own lot with the City before you finalize a design.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does a garage cost in Airdrie?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">BVM Builders advertises $55,000 to $85,000 for a 16 by 20 single and $82,000 to $125,000 for a 22 by 22 double on its Airdrie page, with GST not stated. That is one builder's range, not a quote from this site. Get two or three written quotes with the same scope listed so you can compare them fairly.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 10px;">Does Back Lane Garage Co build the garage?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. This is an advertising site that connects Airdrie homeowners with independent garage builders. The builder who quotes your job contracts directly with you, and the City says Airdrie contractors must hold valid trade qualification certificates and an Airdrie business licence. Ask any builder about both before you sign.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
